// From the journal, not yet reached here (spec): a program that ends is not
// only one that stops asking — every step has to take a finite time, so
// termination is a temporal question, and the language has to be able to ask
// it. Anything done to one thing may be collected into a function, and that
// function drawn as an animation of itself.
